---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const p='/equipment/08-10/',manual='https://nc-p-001.sitecorecontenthub.cloud/api/public/content/ad6ce7f8a8c34b72bd5295efa895fc74?v=b3982c97';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Ultimus V dispensing witness" subtitle="" wide={true} description="Operate a metric inert volume-dispensing example and preserve masked contact openings."><script is:inline>window.dispenseModule=import('/equipment/08-10/dispenser.mjs');</script><article class="equipment" id="disp"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/08-10/">← Equipment 08-10</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#disp-ref">References</a><a href="#disp-proof">Verification</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">08-10 / MICROASSEMBLY</p><h2>Coat the plate. Leave the contacts open.</h2><p class="eq-lede">Fire the seated flat coupon with the virtual footswitch. Check that 460 nL spread across 92 mm² yields a 5 µm film and leaves all four masked cells exposed.</p></header>
<div class="cols"><section><p class="eq-meta">01 / INSTRUMENT</p><h3>Nordson EFD Ultimus V</h3><div id="dp-view" aria-label="Metric controller, stage and foot pedal"></div><small id="dp-model" role="status">Loading model…</small><div class="tools"><button id="dp-whole">Whole bench</button><button id="dp-plate">Syringe and workholder</button><button id="dp-rear">Rear I/O</button></div><p>Drag to orbit; pinch or scroll to zoom. The model’s green cycle key or pedal triggers the same virtual sequence as the button. The map outlines each virtual shot; it is not a claim that the dispenser has an integrated automatic stage.</p></section>
<section><p class="eq-meta">02 / ACTUATION</p><h3>Calibrated volume witness</h3><label>Total programmed volume (virtual nL)<input id="dp-dose" value="460" min="1" max="50000" type="number" step="any"/></label><div class="tools"><button id="dp-fire" class="run">Press virtual pedal</button><button id="dp-stage">Unseat coupon</button><button id="dp-power">Disable controller</button><button id="dp-reset">Reset example</button></div><p id="dp-status" role="status">Inert calibration fixture ready.</p><details><summary>Import a flat raster program</summary><p>Define a rectangular plate, cell pitch, total virtual volume and named openings. <a href={p+'example-program.json'} download>Download sample input</a>.</p><label>Program JSON<input id="dp-import" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"/></label></details></section></div>
<section><p class="eq-meta">03 / HEIGHT MAP</p><h3>Dose recovery and exposed openings</h3><p id="dp-result" aria-live="polite"></p><canvas id="dp-map" width="600" height="290" aria-label="Virtual raster with covered cells, exposed openings, and selected pulse"></canvas><label>Inspect shot along serpentine path<input id="dp-cursor" type="range" min="0" max="0" value="0" disabled/></label><p id="dp-shot"></p><p>Gold identifies programmed contact openings J1 and J2. Their film thickness is exactly zero. A small marker in the workholder tracks the selected shot; it is not extra material.</p><button id="dp-save" disabled>Export shot list and thickness JSON</button></section>
<section id="disp-ref"><p class="eq-meta">04 / SPECIFICATION</p><h3>Part 7012590, with bench accessories</h3><p>The <a href="https://www.nordson.com/en/Products/EFD-Products/Ultimus-V-Dispensers">Nordson EFD product photograph</a> and <a href={manual+'#page=14'}>operating manual p. 14</a> establish the white face, blue keys, display and front fluid-delivery line. <a href={manual+'#page=15'}>Manual p. 15</a> identifies the air input, exhaust, pedal, RS-232, I/O and power connections. No manufacturer images are republished.</p><p>The nominal cabinet width, height and depth are 225 × 95 × 199 mm (<a href={manual+'#page=11'}>manual p. 11</a>), checked in the asset separately from feet and accessories. Syringe/grip/needle stand and footswitch are original inferred geometry; no model-specific needle dimensions or routing claim. The selected 10 mL Optimum-style accessory is illustrative.</p><div class="tools"><a href={p+'build-model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a><a href={p+'ultimus-v.glb'} download>Download GLB</a><a href={p+'xr.json'}>Geometry checks and VR targets</a><a href={p+'dispenser.mjs'}>Solver/action module</a><a href={p+'example-map.json'}>Example export</a></div></section>
<section id="disp-proof"><p class="eq-meta">05 / METHOD & VERIFICATION</p><h3>Conservation before materials</h3><p>The open part of a flat grid is divided into equal, non-overlapping square cells. One pulse per eligible cell carries V/N nL in serpentine order. Since 1 nL equals 1 mm² × 1 µm, the thickness in each eligible cell is (V/N)/pitch². Summing area × thickness recovers the input, while no pulse or thickness is assigned to masked cells. This is an ideal uniform virtual dose, not measured wetting, spread, pneumatic timing, curing, flow, viscosity or void formation.</p><div class="over"><table><thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Expected</th><th>Computed</th><th>Tolerance</th></tr></thead><tbody>{[['Dose reconstruction','460 nL','460 nL'],['Thickness over 92 mm²','5 µm','5 µm'],['Named openings (4 cells)','4 × 0 µm','4 × 0 µm'],['Doubled dose','10 µm','10 µm']].map(([k,e,a])=><tr><th>{k}</th><td>{e}</td><td>{a}</td><td>Pass · 10⁻⁹ in declared units</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><b>Data contract:</b> <code>bts.dispense-raster.v1</code>, flat 1–40 mm square/rectangular dimensions, isotropic pitch 0.25–4 mm, at most 1,600 whole cells, volume 1–50,000 virtual nL. Cell indices start at the lower-left corner; physical XY is plate-centred, +X right, +Y rear. Output <code>bts.encapsulation-map.v1</code> preserves plate/revision, opening IDs, calibration/material IDs, volume, pulse positions and heights, with cure “not modeled” and unknown void probability. No compatible downstream station is assumed. Named metric ray targets support VR reuse; this first-pass page does not verify a headset session.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/08-10/client.mjs';</script><style is:global>
#disp .cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.12fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:.8rem}#disp section{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1rem;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}#disp .cols section{margin:0}#disp h3{margin:.3rem 0 .6rem;font-size:1.5rem}#disp .eq-meta{margin:0}#disp .tools{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.45rem;align-items:center;margin:.65rem 0}#disp label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.3rem}#disp input,#disp button{min-height:40px;padding:.35rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;font:inherit;background:var(--panel,transparent);color:var(--text);border:1px solid var(--border)}#disp button{cursor:pointer}#disp button.run{background:#335e56;color:white}#disp button:disabled{opacity:.45}#dp-view{height:clamp(260px,30vw,400px);background:#26363a}#dp-view canvas{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;touch-action:none}#dp-map{width:min(100%,670px);height:auto;display:block}#disp .over{overflow:auto}#disp table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}#disp th,#disp td{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}#dp-result{font-weight:bold}@media(max-width:760px){#disp .cols{grid-template-columns:1fr}#disp section{padding:.7rem}}
</style>
